# Line-ending policy.
#
# Five consecutive plans in phase 01 hit the same Windows symptom: a regenerated
# file reports as modified while being byte-identical, and every `git add` emits
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings. Declaring the policy here makes the
# repository's stored form explicit instead of leaving it to each machine's
# core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Everything git detects as text is stored with LF. Working-tree line endings are
# left to the platform; only the committed form is normalised.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated data snapshots. These are compared byte-for-byte by the roster and
# sprite build scripts to prove regeneration is idempotent, so their stored form
# must be stable.
*.json text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf

# Binary assets — the committed sprite set. Never transform these.
*.png binary
